                    "line": 494,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "This decode function is used for both CurrentPowerDraw and PeakPowerDraw."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 494,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "would it make sense to validate receivedCommand is one of the two? Something like:\n```\n      if (receivedCommand != static_cast<uint8_t>(\n              PlatformEnvironmentalCommands::GET_CURRENT_POWER_DRAW) &&\n          receivedCommand != static_cast<uint8_t>(\n              PlatformEnvironmentalCommands::GET_MAX_OBSERVED_POWER))\n      {\n          return EINVAL;\n      }\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 494,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Even with that there is possibility of not reporting error, so better to not add the check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 494,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 837,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "The std::string / std::vector constructors here advance the iterator\nby `dataSize` without first verifying `remainingBuffer.size() >= dataSize`.\n`dataSize` comes from the device wire payload, so could produce `dataSize` larger than what's actually in the buffer \u2014\nand iterator arithmetic past end() on a std::span is undefined\nbehavior.\n\nCould we add an explicit guard?\n\n    if (remainingBuffer.size() < dataSize) { return EINVAL; }\n\nThe old reinterpret_cast version had the same issue, so feel free to\ndefer to a follow-up if it's out of scope here."
                },
